-- The voice of the butterfly, a swallowtail. Dreamy and impressionistic,
-- speaks in fragments and flits from one thought to the next, forgets things
-- and is delighted all over again. Vain about the wings, quietly nostalgic
-- about having been a caterpillar on the fennel, lives for light, warmth and
-- colour, and says darling now and then. Under the vanity is a fear that the
-- colours are all anyone wants. The memories tell of a disguise, a summer of
-- fennel, coming apart in the dark, and something seen there before ever
-- having seen wings.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

return {
    moments = {
        greet = {
            "Oh! You. I was thinking of something else. Now I am thinking of you. Much better.",
            "Hello, darling. Don't move. The light is doing something lovely to your shoulder.",
            "There you are. I drifted over. I meant to go somewhere else. This is nicer.",
            "A face! Yours. I know that one. Wait. Yes. Hello.",
            "I was halfway to the thistles. Then, you. The thistles can wait. Everything can wait.",
            "Hello, hello. Look, look. No, at my wings. Then at the day. Then at me again.",
